details:
WINNER ALGORITHM PSEUDO-CODE (firmware-precise; replaces the integrate-and-clamp block in PID_controller, step2 semantics otherwise unchanged):
constants: GATE_HOLDOFF=3125 (0.1 s), GATE_DEADBAND=1000 counts, I_BASE=authority>>2 (existing), I_FULL=authority;
state (4x int32, zeroed on PID reset): prev_sign, same_ticks, freeze_ticks, last_cross_i;
per tick, after the max_error clamp of error:
  s = (error > GATE_DEADBAND) ? 1 : (error < -GATE_DEADBAND) ? -1 : 0;
  crossed = 0;
  if (s != 0) { if (s == prev_sign) { if (same_ticks < GATE_HOLDOFF) same_ticks++; } else { crossed = (prev_sign != 0); prev_sign = s; same_ticks = 0; } }   // s==0 (inside deadband): hold all state
  limit = (same_ticks >= GATE_HOLDOFF) ? I_FULL : I_BASE;
  if (crossed) { tmp = integral_term; integral_term = (int32)(((int64)integral_term + last_cross_i) >> 1); last_cross_i = tmp; freeze_ticks = GATE_HOLDOFF; }
  if (freeze_ticks > 0) { freeze_ticks--; /* I holds */ }
  else { ni = integral_term + error*ki;   /* int32-safe: |I|<=I_FULL, |error*ki| <= INT32_MAX - I_FULL by the ki cap */
         if (ni > limit)       { if (ni < integral_term) integral_term = ni; else if (integral_term < limit) integral_term = limit; /* else hold excess */ }
         else if (ni < -limit) { if (ni > integral_term) integral_term = ni; else if (integral_term > -limit) integral_term = -limit; }
         else integral_term = ni; }
back-calculation (existing saturation path): clamp new_i to +/-I_FULL instead of +/-I_BASE (clamping to I_BASE would slam a legitimately wound I on a transient D-spike saturation; observed in freeze-mode traces).
Per-tick cost: typical path ~10-15 extra instructions (2 cmp sign, cmp+inc counter, 1 cmp limit select, 2-4 extra cmp in limit logic, 1 cmp+dec freeze) out of a 2,048-cycle budget at 64 MHz/31.25 kHz (<1%); crossing path (+~8 instr) is rare. No divisions, no floats; one int64 add for the midpoint (or int32, safe by the bound below).
